WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.460
- [Narrator] The universe is everything.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.113
From the tiniest particles,

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.913
to the largest galaxies,

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.513
to the very existence of
space, time, and life.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.923
But how did it all begin?

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.860
The origin of the universe
is the origin of everything.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.310
Multiple scientific theories

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.200
plus creation myths from around the world

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.060
have tried to explain
its mysterious genesis.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.320
However, the most widely
accepted explanation

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.123
is the Big Bang theory.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.180
The Big Bang theory states
that the universe began

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.110
as a hot and infinitely dense point.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.920
Only a few millimeters
wide, it was similar

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.143
to a supercharged black hole.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.480
About 13.7 billion years ago

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.113
this tiny singularity violently exploded.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.520
And it is from this explosion, this bang,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.543
that all matter, energy,
space, and time were created.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.530
What happened next were two major stages

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.140
of the universe's evolution.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.520
Called the radiation and matter eras,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.590
they're defined by key events

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.533
that helped shape the universe.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.850
First came the radiation era,

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.940
named for the dominance of radiation

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.473
right after the Big Bang.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.960
This era is made of
smaller stages call epochs

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.730
that occurred within the universe's

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.883
first tens of thousands of years.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.820
The earliest is the Planck epoch.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.880
No matter existed in the
universe at this time,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.900
only energy and the ancestor

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.530
to the four forces of
nature, the superforce.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.360
At the end of this stage, however,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.300
a key event occurred in which gravity

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.523
split away from the superforce.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.470
Next came the grand unification epoch,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.510
named for the three remaining
unified forces of nature.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:08.080
This epoch ended when one of those forces,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.283
called strong, or strong
nuclear, broke away.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.470
Then the inflationary epoch began

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.060
during which the universe
rapidly expanded.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.310
Almost instantly it grew
from the size of an atom

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.233
to the size of a grapefruit.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.270
The universe at this time was piping hot

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:32.053
and it churned with electrons,
quarks, and other particles.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.500
Then came the electroweak epoch,

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.510
when the last two forces,
electromagnetic and weak,

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.910
finally split off.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.620
During the next stage, the quark epoch,

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.400
all of the universe's
ingredients were present,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.000
however, the universe was
still too hot and dense

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.163
for subatomic particles to form.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.950
Then, in the hadron epoch, the
universe cooled down enough

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.963
for quarks to bind together
and form protons and neutrons.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.240
In the lepton and nuclear epics,

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.870
the radiation era's last two stages,

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.640
the protons and neutrons
underwent a significant change.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.540
They fused and created nuclei.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.880
And in doing so, they created the first

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.893
chemical element in the universe, helium.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.560
The universe's new
ability to form elements,

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.300
the building blocks of matter,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.963
queued the matter era.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:33.190
Much as the name suggests,
the matter era's defined

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.820
by the presence and predominance

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.000
of matter in the universe.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.630
It features three epochs
that span billions of years.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.400
The vast majority of the
universe's life span,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.800
and includes the present day.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.210
The first was the atomic epoch.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.520
In this stage, the universe's temperature

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.380
cooled down enough for electrons

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.943
to attach to nuclei for the first time.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.870
Called recombination,
this process helped create

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.773
the universe's second element, hydrogen.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.720
This hydrogen, along with helium atoms,

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.030
dotted the universe with atomic clouds.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.960
Within the clouds, small pockets of gas

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.510
may have had enough gravity
to cause atoms to collect.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:19.270
These clusters of atoms, formed
during the galactic epoch,

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:22.570
became the seedlings of galaxies.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.720
Nestled inside those
galaxies, stars began to form.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.180
And in doing so, they queued the latest

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.290
and current stage of the
universe's development,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.433
the stellar epoch.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.980
The formation of stars then caused

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.790
a tremendous ripple effect

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.930
and helped shape the
universe as we know it.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.350
Heat within the stars
caused the conversion

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.420
of helium and hydrogen into almost all

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.763
the remaining elements in the universe.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.680
In turn, those elements
became the building blocks

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:02.103
for planets, moons, life,

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.163
everything we see today.

00:05:07.931 --> 00:05:10.730
This ecosystem of
everything was only possible

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.883
because of the many stages in
the universe's development.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.640
While countless questions
about the origins

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.130
of our universe remain,
it's only a matter of time

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.373
for some long-sought answers to emerge.

